  "defects": [
    "Manual saved takes were not reserved, and onplay required a deliveryState property that older takes can lack. The old claimed-only marker did not consume ready/manual takes.",
    "A failed onplay marker left a claimed take that startup restored to ready, allowing automatic heard-news replay.",
    "Automatic canonical-URL exclusion was not checked atomically against claimed/started/played variants.",
    "Post-claim validation failures could strand a reservation without returning its identity.",
    "News failures shared music Retry/Skip controls and their explanation disappeared during automatic song load."
  ],
  "decision": {
    "protocol": "Reserve ready saved take with a unique claim token; save started before invoking voice.play. Exact token guards start/mark/release. Actual onplay alone sets session Last heard and requests final played marker. Audition does not reserve or consume.",
    "manualReplay": "Explicit manual scheduling of started/played returns unchanged consumed state and bypasses an eligibility lease. Cancel never makes consumed news ready.",
    "cancellation": "Release exact claimed, or exact started only when this player explicitly knows play was never invoked. Pause/rewind retain schedule; late gate results respect token/object/attempt/phase/track/play intent. Audio owner cleanup also cancels delivery.",
    "restart": "Token-bearing unstarted claim becomes ready; started/played remains consumed. Legacy tokenless claimed is conservatively started because an older player may already have spoken before marker failure.",
    "reservation": "Automatic CAS excludes canonical URLs in claimed/started/played; manual new lease rejects active claimed overlap. Explicit manual replay remains intentional. Failed final verification releases only its exact lease; failed cleanup reports original context and restart guidance.",
    "feedback": "Separate non-actionable DJ status above player persists through automatic continuation and clears next explicit music command or new schedule. Marker errors respect a revision captured at onplay. Saved audio explains uncertain started history without asserting that audio was heard.",
    "tradeoff": "Disk history and sound cannot commit atomically. Crash after durable start but before sound can omit unheard news; avoid automatic replay and leave explicit saved replay available. No exactly-once sound guarantee."
  },
  "review": {
    "backend": "Independent Boris/Nadia proposals and challenge settled token leases/durable start. Nadia found and Boris fixed final-read release leak and atomic consumed-URL race; final review found no blocker and independently reran the original68 checks. Added dual-failure cleanup case subsequently passes.",
    "frontend": "Independent Steve/Elena proposals and challenge settled pause/rewind/cancel behavior. Steve found missing audio-owner cleanup release; fixed. Both endorsed separate DJ notice after native failure reproduction; actual final logic review found no blocker. Marker wording refined from played to started.",
    "alternative": "Consumed manual replay bypasses the eligible lease without changing persisted state, rather than storing/restoring prior state. Shared recovery/history remains separate from Last heard."
  },
  "service": {
    "method": "Bundle actual prepared-news/service dependencies, substitute Electron userData and local-state/key adapters. Eleven fresh processes use real temp files and actual queued atomic index writes/renames. Synthetic3-byte audio tests service availability only, not decoding. A fixture checkpoint before automatic CAS forces competing start; controlled final-state read hooks and a directory at the target index force write/release failures. No UI, provider dispatch or external server.",
